<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greater Kabylia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Great Kabylia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabylia">Kabylia</a> is the mountainous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djurdjura">Djurdjura</a> range, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>, with Tizi Ouzou as its main town today. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cabyle">Kabyle</a> villages long kept strong self-government. In the 16th century it was the base of the Kingdom of Kuku, and it resisted French conquest until 1857, rising again in 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greater-kabylia.jpg" alt="Greater Kabylia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: IRRIGATIONDZ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DJURDJURA6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
